# Architecture Rules

## Project

This is a production-grade AI skincare commerce and automation platform.

The application must prioritize:

* Security
* Data integrity
* Maintainability
* Testability
* Clear domain boundaries
* Production reliability

Do not optimize for rapid code generation at the expense of architecture.

---

## Technology

Use:

* Next.js
* TypeScript
* PostgreSQL
* Prisma
* Redis
* BullMQ
* Tailwind CSS
* shadcn/ui
* Zod

Do not introduce another framework or ORM without explicit justification.

---

## Domain Architecture

Organize backend logic by business domain.

Preferred structure:

```text
src/modules/

auth/
tenants/
users/
customers/
products/
cart/
checkout/
orders/
payments/
leads/
conversations/
ai/
automations/
notifications/
analytics/
```

Each module should separate:

```text
validation
types
services
repositories
tests
```

Do not place business logic directly inside React components.

Do not put large amounts of business logic inside route handlers.

---

## Request Architecture

Use:

```text
Request
 ↓
Authentication
 ↓
Authorization
 ↓
Validation
 ↓
Service
 ↓
Repository
 ↓
Database
```

Route handlers should be thin.

---

## Database

PostgreSQL is the source of truth.

Prisma is the primary database access layer.

Do not use Redis as a permanent source of business data.

Do not duplicate authoritative business state across systems unnecessarily.

---

## Multi-Tenancy

All tenant-owned resources must be tenant-scoped.

Never retrieve a tenant-owned resource using only its ID when the current tenant context is available.

Prefer:

```text
getProduct(productId, tenantId)
```

over:

```text
getProduct(productId)
```

